# ztd environment template: user secrets and user-specific endpoints only.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a        export it into the shell that runs ./ztd
#
# ztd reads environment variables only through the typed keys in
# protocol/constants/env_vars.json (INV-ENV-04, docs/devs/devs.md); a key that
# is not in that registry is never read. Every secret and user_endpoint key in
# the registry is listed below as a commented entry with its purpose, its
# consumer, whether the default flow needs it, and an example value
# (`make constants-check` enforces this). No key is required for the default
# flow (make up, make gw, make operator, ./ztd ...).
#
# Secret keys are withheld from governed child processes
# (constants.SecretEnvVars). A variable that is not in the registry, exported
# from this file, is inherited by every governed command: keep only registry
# keys here.
#
# Platform configuration (ports, listen host, service URLs, passkey and CORS
# origins, consensus, doctrine and vault paths, Ollama endpoint, models) is
# never an env setting: it is a typed default or a flag
# (`./ztd <command> --help`). Provider API keys and web search are configured in
# platform settings. The master key is selected with --master-key-file.

# =============================================================================
# Cloudflare (optional)
# =============================================================================
# Purpose: Cloudflare API token with DNS edit permission on the zone that routes the tunnel hostname; --api-token overrides it.
# Consumer: ./ztd gw tunnel route-dns (docs/guides/cloudflare_tunnel.md).
# Required for default flow: no
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-cloudflare-api-token
